The attached image illustrates immunofluorescence microscopy of skeletal muscle 24 hours post-injection, showing the in vivo effects of Nano-11 and soluble ovalbumin (OVA). The top row (Nano-11 + OVA) reveals significant infiltration of Mac-2+ monocytes/macrophages and MHCII+ cells, many of which contain intracellular red-labeled Nano-11. This indicates Nano-11's ability to induce a local inflammatory response and efficient uptake by antigen-presenting cells. The bottom row (OVA only) shows very few inflammatory cells, highlighting the adjuvant effect of Nano-11 in recruiting immune cells to the injection site.